Working on a project as such has been a truly stimulating experience: for starters, I got to explore the potential design of an app that I have extensively used for years as addition to my language studies – and, to me personally, provided great value already as it is in its current shape, thanks to its precious content.

More importantly, though, this case study allowed me to expand on my UI skills built throughout my career as a designer, and see firsthand how they fit in a much bigger – and holistic – picture;

Using AI to overcome external limitations – due to the lack of access to real-life data, given the educational nature of the project – has helped me reduce personal bias and treat my own experience as a user as complementary information – not as “source of truth”, in my design choices.
